<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- A floating CONTROL capsule on the flight screen. Specification §4.2.

     WHAT IT REPLACED: a solid bar across the WHOLE width (bg_toolbar). It was opaque chrome over
     the one thing the pilot flies from, and once the HUD readouts lost their panels it was the
     only element left still separating itself with a solid background.

     The controls now sit in two capsules that float on the video — status on the left, actions
     on the right — and the strip between them is picture again.

     WHY A FILL HERE AND AN OUTLINE ON THE READOUTS: a capsule covers a small patch, so it can
     afford to be opaque, and the icons inside it keep their own colours (green for connected,
     red for live, amber for caution) which an outline would fight. The readouts cover far more
     of the picture and carry no colour of their own, so they take the outline instead.

     ⚠ THE RADIUS IS THE LARGE ONE ON PURPOSE. hud_control_radius says "you touch this"; the
     small hud_pill_radius says "you read this" — the pills inside, the mini-map frame. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/tp_hud_capsule" />
    <corners android:radius="@dimen/hud_control_radius" />
</shape>
